<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saw Yun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1315">1315</a>–<a href="/years/1327">1327</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saw Yun was the founder of the Sagaing Kingdom in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-burma">Upper Burma</a>. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thihathu">Thihathu</a>, ruler of Pinya, he quarrelled with his father and in 1315 set up his own court at Sagaing, across the Irrawaddy, which became a rival to Pinya for half a century. He ruled until his death in 1327; the two kingdoms were united in 1364 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thado-minbya">Thado Minbya</a> founded Ava.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saw-yun.jpg" alt="Saw Yun" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cepyita · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Athinkhayasawyun.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
